    "intro_html":  "Real Hungarian gulyas is not the macaroni skillet the school cafeteria called goulash. It is a slow paprika braise, chuck roast and onions cooked down until the sauce turns deep red and the potatoes go soft at the edges. Each bowl lands at 600 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e45 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$5.00 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e. The pot does the work. You mostly stir and wait.",
